<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diet of Worms</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1521</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Diet of Worms (1521)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Diet of Worms was the imperial assembly held in 1521 by the young Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> at Worms. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> appeared before it and refused to recant his writings. The resulting Edict of Worms declared him an outlaw and banned his works, but it was poorly enforced, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> spread in the following years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diet-of-worms.jpg" alt="Diet of Worms" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton von Werner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9B%D1%8E%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80_%D0%B2_%D0%92%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BC%D1%81%D0%B5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
